11
00:47:48,461 --> 00:47:54,461
The Maze Runner is a 2014 American dystopian science fiction film directed by Wes Ball,
in his feature directorial debut, based on James Dashner's 2009 novel.

12
00:52:09,230 --> 00:52:15,230
It is the first installment in The Maze Runner film series and was
produced by Noah Oppenheim, Grant Pierce Myers and T.

13
00:56:30,000 --> 00:56:36,000
The film stars Dylan O'Brien, Kaya Scodelario, Thomas
Brodie-Sangster, Will Poulter and Patricia Clarkson.

14
01:00:50,769 --> 01:00:56,769
The story follows sixteen-year-old Thomas, portrayed by O'Brien, who awakens in a rusty elevator with no memory of who he is, only to learn that he has been delivered to the middle of an intricate
maze, along with many other boys, who have been trying to find their way out of the ever-changing labyrinth—all while establishing a functioning society in what they call the Glade.

15
01:05:11,538 --> 01:05:17,538
Development of The Maze Runner began in January 2011 when Fox purchased the film rights to Dashner's novel with
Gotham Group and Temple Hill Entertainment as producers and Catherine Hardwicke intended to direct.

16
01:09:32,307 --> 01:09:38,307
In 2012, Ball was hired to direct the film adaptation after presenting an animated short film titled
Ruin with a similar tone and was initially considered for a feature-length adaptation.

17
01:13:53,076 --> 01:13:59,076
Principal photography began in Baton Rouge, Louisiana on May 13,
2013, and officially concluded on July 12, 2013.

18
01:18:13,846 --> 01:18:19,846
The Maze Runner was released on September 19, 2014, in
the United States by 20th Century Fox.

19
01:22:34,615 --> 01:22:40,615
The film received positive reviews, with praise for Ball's
direction, the actors' performances and the film's tone.

20
01:26:55,384 --> 01:27:01,384
Critics considered it to be better than most young
adult book-to-film adaptations.

21
01:31:16,153 --> 01:31:22,153
The film was first at the box office in its opening weekend, grossing $32.5
million, making it the seventh-highest-grossing debut in September.

22
01:35:36,923 --> 01:35:42,923
The film earned over $348 million worldwide at the box
office, against its budget of $34 million.

23
01:39:57,692 --> 01:40:03,692
Two sequels, Maze Runner: The Scorch Trials and Maze Runner:
The Death Cure, were released in 2015 and 2018.

24
01:44:18,461 --> 01:44:24,461
The film explores themes of based on novel or book, escape,
dystopia, maze, post-apocalyptic future.

25
01:48:39,230 --> 01:48:45,230
The tone is intense and thought_provoking and mind_bending.
